{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Landed + replicated\n\nGerrit change 1429 merged to main (rebased on submit). Both gates were green before Submit:\nLLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, with zero unresolved comments.\n\nReplication on merged main: the original report no longer reproduces. Re-running the\nsynthetic reproduction of the false-negative -- an inert `CodeHealthConfig.enabled` beside a\nlive `UiConfig.enabled` -- now yields exactly one error naming `CodeHealthConfig.enabled`,\nwhere the pre-fix gate reported only the unrelated section-wiring field and let the inert one\nthrough. The real tree passes the gate (`Config-read gate: OK`) and both gate test files pass\n(27/27).\n\nResidual risk and prevention:\n- The resolver keys function names bare (module-agnostic), so a same-named function in another\n  module can only WIDEN a binding. That direction is fail-quiet -- it can suppress a firing but\n  never invent one -- so it cannot break CI on a live field. Accepted, and documented in the\n  script's module docstring.\n- An unresolvable receiver credits no field, which is fail-LOUD. That risk was retired\n  empirically rather than by assertion: the whole tree was swept and all four newly-flagged\n  fields were traced by hand to real consumers. Accepted.\n- No marker in the schema currently names a ticket id, so there is no marker parked against a\n  closed ticket. Reported, nothing to file.\n- No sibling instances of the construct were found in the other gate scripts, and the gate has\n  a single surface (the Config-read CI step), so the parity census has no MISSING slot."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785919397590113001,"uuid":"200f05c6-1a69-406d-9d7d-2bf254accf49"}